{
 "notes": {
  "_about": "offset-map.md, Window check: what the phone measured on 2026-11-20 (YT Clients chat, scratchpad offset-test/result.txt), as numbers; the audio is not kept. Per song: YouTube's copy and the copy the user's addons gave, both decoded to mono 22 050 Hz; a 12 s addon window every 30 s from 15 s, read at YouTube's position (the audition's same-position read).",
  "expect": "A port running the window check on the same two copies must give each window's verdict (match or refuse) and, for a match, offsetMs within 1 ms. coarse and fine are the scores measured then, for reference: the phone's run compared YouTube's span against the window; the rule now slides the window over YouTube's copy (it holds for offsets of seconds), which can move a score by a little but not across 0.8 on these copies.",
  "copies": "Escapism (A7Zlgi2FMUE) and the Stereo Love smashup (exHJb5t-6e8): the addons' copies are other recordings or edits (the full fit refuses them too), so every window must refuse. Poker Face (oG-4Uvhm4lI): the lossless copy is -117.2 ms off YouTube's in every window.",
  "rebuild": "Local only, git-ignored, never in CI; nothing is downloaded without the user's word. YouTube's side: ffmpeg -i .cache/analysis/<id>.wav -ac 1 -ar 22050 -f f32le .cache/addons/<id>.yt.f32 (the analysis cache's decode). The addon side: the song's lossless copy from the user's addons (scripts/addon_window_fetch.mjs <file of addon links> .cache/addons), then ffmpeg -i .cache/addons/<id>.audio -ac 1 -ar 22050 -f f32le .cache/addons/<id>.ad.f32. Run: node scripts/addon_window_cases.mjs."
 },
